# Python + Pony ORM Core Conventions (Project Rules)

## Architecture boundaries
- Keep DB access inside a dedicated persistence layer (repositories/DAO/services), not sprinkled throughout handlers, CLI, or UI code.
- Never perform DB I/O at import time. Imports must be side-effect free.

## Model organization
- Place Pony Entities under `app/models/`.
- One Entity class per file.
- No circular imports between models. Prefer Pony string references in relationships when needed.

## Transactions
- Every DB read/write must occur inside a `db_session` (decorator or context manager).
- Keep transactions short; do not hold a session across slow I/O (network calls, file writes).

## Schema evolution
- For local dev/tests you may use `generate_mapping(create_tables=True)`.
- For production, prefer explicit schema management (migrations or controlled DDL), and avoid auto-creating tables.

## Coding standards
- Prefer explicit imports (avoid `import *`) and type hints on public functions.
- Raise domain-specific exceptions at the boundary (service layer) and log context once, close to the caller.
